      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Absence of right coronary artery is a rare coronary anomaly that may present with myocardial ischemia. This is a case report of a 49-year-old female with chest pain and positive stress test. Coronary angiogram revealed absence of right coronary artery with normal left coronary system."},
